= December 2022 — A gift, an office and a hole in the wall

The Chief of Police, **Jarosław Szymczyk**, returns from Ukraine with two
grenade launchers presented to him by his Ukrainian counterparts. In his own
office in national headquarters, one of them fires. The blast damages the
building; a civilian employee is treated. The first official account calls it
an unspecified incident. The second calls it an accident with a gift. The third
concedes that the head of the Polish police brought live ordnance into a
government building and discharged it there.

Nobody died, which is why the country is laughing. The institutional facts are
not funny: the commander of a national police force handled a weapon he could
not identify, in a building full of staff, and the organisation's first
instinct was to describe it vaguely.

He offers to resign. The interior minister declines to accept it.

[? if office_misuse_register = 1: The asset register we forced through in 2019
covers official travel and gifts, which is the only reason the launchers appear
in a document at all.?]
[? if police_trust < 45: Public confidence in the police was already low before
a launcher went off in its headquarters.?]

- @szymczyk_oversight
- @szymczyk_resign
- @szymczyk_mock

@szymczyk_oversight
title: Use it to demand civilian oversight of police command
subtitle: Requires an asset and conduct register to build on. Turns a farce into the oversight structure the force has never had.
choose-if: office_misuse_register = 1 or nik_referral_channel = 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have neither a conduct register nor an audit channel — an oversight demand now is a headline with no mechanism behind it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.szymczyk_response = "Civilian oversight";
Q.police_oversight_pressure =
    (Number(Q.police_oversight_pressure) || 0) + 15;
Q.police_trust = (Number(Q.police_trust) || 40) + 5;
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 6;
Q.administrative_reform_pressure =
    (Number(Q.administrative_reform_pressure) || 0) + 4;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.constitutional_restraint =
    (Number(Q.constitutional_restraint) || 0) + 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "The launcher becomes an argument for civilian oversight of the police";
!}

Our demand is not for his head. It is for the thing the Polish police has never
had: an independent body that reviews command conduct, publishes findings and
cannot be closed by the minister whose appointee it is examining.

Serving officers, who have spent a decade watching political appointments
arrive above them, are unexpectedly supportive. The structure does not get
built this year. It is on the table every time an officer is filmed doing
something the ministry then describes vaguely, which is often.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@szymczyk_resign
title: Demand the resignation and let the minister own the refusal
subtitle: Simple, correct and it ends when he stays.
on-arrival: {!
Q.szymczyk_response = "Resignation demanded";
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 2;
Q.pis_relation = (Number(Q.pis_relation) || 0) - 5;
Q.police_trust = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.police_trust) || 40) - 2
);
Q.left_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.05;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left demands the police commander resign and the minister refuses";
!}

He offered. The minister refused. We ask, in the chamber, what a commander
would have to do to be replaced, and receive no answer that survives being read
back.

The exchange lasts a week. Szymczyk remains in post until the government
changes, and the precedent that a national commander cannot be removed for
this stands with him.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@szymczyk_mock
title: Let the joke do the work
subtitle: Free, enormous reach, and it teaches the country that police accountability is a comedy segment.
on-arrival: {!
Q.szymczyk_response = "Ridicule";
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 4;
Q.left_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.15;
Q.police_trust = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.police_trust) || 40) - 5
);
Q.institutional_trust = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) - 3
);
Q.covid_anti_system_pressure =
    (Number(Q.covid_anti_system_pressure) || 0) + 4;
Q.news_headline =
    "The headquarters explosion becomes the funniest week of the year";
!}

We do not have to do anything. The material writes itself and our accounts have
their best week since the pandemic.

What the week actually establishes is that the national police command is a
subject for jokes rather than for oversight, and that nothing follows from
either. The next time an officer is filmed doing something serious, the same
audience is already primed to treat it as content.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue
